        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="STA02" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Baroness</roleName>
                        <forename>Germaine</forename>
                        <surname>Stael von Holstein</surname>
                        <addName> Anne-Louise, née Necker, Germaine de Stael</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1766-04-22">
                        <placeName>France</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1817-07-14"/>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <occupation>intellectual</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Mme de Stael visits England in 1813. Her former lover Benjamin Constant
    had begun a translation of <title>Political Justice</title> that was not completed and there is a suggestion
    that they had collaborated on this. It is notable that when Constant visits England 18 months
    later he does not meet Godwin and probably does not attempt to visit him - it is likely that Mme de Stael's correspondence 
    gave clear guidance on who was, or was not, worth meeting!</p>
                        <p>Godwin also notes her death.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
